Digital Design and Computer Architecture, Harris, David; Harris, Sara 
Day 1

Chapter 1
The driver produces a LOW (0) output in the range of 0 to V OL or a HIGH (1) output in the range of V OH to V DD . If the receiver gets an input in the range of 0 to V IL , it will consider the input to be LOW. If the receiver gets an input in the range of V IH to V DD , it will consider the input to be HIGH. If, for some reason such as noise or faulty components, the receiver’s input should fall in the forbidden zone between V IL and V IH , the behavior of the gate is unpredictable. V OH , V OL , V IH , and V IL are called the output and input high and low logic levels.

Noice margins:
NM(L) = V (IL) - V (OL)
NM(H) = V (OH) - V (IH)


